SWE-Ladder
Copyright 2026 The SWE-Ladder Authors

This product includes software developed as a research extension of several
open-source projects. Nothing here is a redistribution of a complete upstream
project: the upstream trees are cloned by the user and modified in place by
`integration/install.sh`.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWE-Master  (https://github.com/RUCAIBox/SWE-Master)

    One repository that vendors both the rllm RL trainer (DeepSWE_RL/rllm) and
    the R2E-Gym agent scaffold (R2E-Gym/). Our work is built on top of it, at
    commit fb864a7d397b2c287ba6e38152da2228efc98e03.

    Derived from it and carrying its license, not ours:

      integration/patches/rllm-swe-ladder.patch
      integration/patches/r2egym-swe-ladder.patch
          Diffs against those two trees. The hunks are our changes; the files
          they land in remain upstream works.

      swe_ladder/prompt_templates_openhands/
          Generated from R2E-Gym's src/r2egym/agenthub/config/openhands/*.yaml
          by scripts/tools/gen_openhands_prompt_templates.py. The system prompt
          and tool descriptions are upstream text, split into per-stage files.

    Consult the upstream repository for its license terms before redistributing
    any of these.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
verl  (https://github.com/verl-project/verl)
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

    A separate repository nested inside rllm, at commit
    d4399a673ae60748271af009d38e9a3dca86086b.
    `integration/patches/verl-swe-ladder.patch` is a diff against it; applying
    it produces a modified copy of an Apache-2.0 work.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Our own code

    `swe_ladder/` (apart from the generated prompt templates noted above),
    `scripts/`, `analysis/`, `stage_capability_eval/`, `eval/`, `training/`,
    `integration/install.sh` and `integration/check_install.py` are new code
    written for this project and licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    as stated in LICENSE. A file adapted from an upstream project says so in its
    own header.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Datasets

    No dataset is redistributed here. `scripts/data/` builds the training and
    evaluation data from the public upstream datasets listed in `data/README.md`
    (SWE-bench/SWE-smith, nebius/SWE-rebench, R2E-Gym/R2E-Gym-Subset,
    SWE-Gym/SWE-Gym, princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Verified), each of which carries
    its own license and terms.

    `data/samples/stages/` holds five instances in the staged record format, as
    runnable examples of that format. Their issue text and gold patches come
    from the datasets above; the repositories they are drawn from
    (0b01001001/spectree, 12rambau/sepal_ui, David-Wobrock/sqlvalidator,
    CSCfi/swift-browser-ui) are public and carry their own licenses.

    `data/stage_router_gold/` is our own annotation work: the step labels are
    ours, the trajectory text they label was generated by our policy inside
    containers built from the datasets above.
